# style.css Cache Busting

All HTML pages link `style.css` with a version query param (e.g. `style.css?v=1.2`).

## Before considering CSS work done

1. **If you modified `style.css`:** Increment the version in every HTML file that links it (`index.html`, `design-system/index.html`, `sightline/index.html`, `sightline-lived-out/index.html`, `seam-field-guide/index.html`, `verdict/index.html`, `verdict/mca/index.html`, and any future pages). Keep the same version across all pages.
2. **If you only changed HTML** (no `style.css` edits): Do not bump the version.
3. **Version format:** Use semantic increments (`1.2` → `1.3`) or integer bumps (`2` → `3`). Stay consistent with the current value in `index.html`.

## Checklist

- [ ] `style.css` change is complete
- [ ] Every `<link href="style.css?v=…">` in `*.html` uses the new version
- [ ] No stale references to deleted stylesheets (e.g. `seam-field-guide.css`)

## Why

GitHub Pages and browsers cache static CSS aggressively. Without a bumped query param, visitors may see stale styles after deploy.
